# gRPC Best Practices

## Error Handling with gRPC Status Codes
Always use appropriate gRPC status codes based on [proto/user.proto](mdc:proto/user.proto) service definitions:

```go
import (
    "google.golang.org/grpc/codes"
    "google.golang.org/grpc/status"
)

// Error mapping examples
func mapDomainError(err error) error {
    switch {
    case errors.Is(err, domain.ErrUserNotFound):
        return status.Errorf(codes.NotFound, "user not found: %v", err)
    case errors.Is(err, domain.ErrInvalidInput):
        return status.Errorf(codes.InvalidArgument, "invalid input: %v", err)
    case errors.Is(err, domain.ErrUserAlreadyExists):
        return status.Errorf(codes.AlreadyExists, "user already exists: %v", err)
    case errors.Is(err, domain.ErrUnauthorized):
        return status.Errorf(codes.Unauthenticated, "unauthorized: %v", err)
    default:
        return status.Errorf(codes.Internal, "internal error: %v", err)
    }
}
```

## Context Handling
Always respect context cancellation and timeouts:

```go
func (h *UserHandler) GetUser(ctx context.Context, req *pb.GetUserRequest) (*pb.GetUserResponse, error) {
    // Check if context is already cancelled
    if ctx.Err() != nil {
        return nil, status.Errorf(codes.Cancelled, "request cancelled")
    }
    
    user, err := h.usecase.GetUser(ctx, req.Id)
    if err != nil {
        return nil, mapDomainError(err)
    }
    
    return &pb.GetUserResponse{User: h.adapter.ToProto(user)}, nil
}
```

## Input Validation
Validate all input at the handler level:

```go
func validateCreateUserRequest(req *pb.CreateUserRequest) error {
    if req.User == nil {
        return status.Errorf(codes.InvalidArgument, "user cannot be nil")
    }
    if req.User.Name == "" {
        return status.Errorf(codes.InvalidArgument, "user name is required")
    }
    if req.User.Email == "" {
        return status.Errorf(codes.InvalidArgument, "user email is required")
    }
    return nil
}
```

## Interceptors for Cross-Cutting Concerns
Implement middleware using gRPC interceptors:

### Logging Interceptor
```go
func LoggingInterceptor(logger *log.Logger) grpc.UnaryServerInterceptor {
    return func(ctx context.Context, req interface{}, info *grpc.UnaryServerInfo, handler grpc.UnaryHandler) (interface{}, error) {
        start := time.Now()
        
        resp, err := handler(ctx, req)
        
        duration := time.Since(start)
        status := codes.OK
        if err != nil {
            status = status.Code(err)
        }
        
        logger.Printf("gRPC call: %s, duration: %v, status: %v", info.FullMethod, duration, status)
        
        return resp, err
    }
}
```

### Recovery Interceptor
```go
func RecoveryInterceptor(logger *log.Logger) grpc.UnaryServerInterceptor {
    return func(ctx context.Context, req interface{}, info *grpc.UnaryServerInfo, handler grpc.UnaryHandler) (resp interface{}, err error) {
        defer func() {
            if r := recover(); r != nil {
                logger.Printf("panic in gRPC handler %s: %v", info.FullMethod, r)
                err = status.Errorf(codes.Internal, "internal server error")
            }
        }()
        
        return handler(ctx, req)
    }
}
```

## Server Configuration in [cmd/commands/start.go](mdc:cmd/commands/start.go)
Enhance the start command with proper interceptors and options:

```go
func createGRPCServer(container *config.Container) *grpc.Server {
    opts := []grpc.ServerOption{
        grpc.ChainUnaryInterceptor(
            LoggingInterceptor(container.Logger),
            RecoveryInterceptor(container.Logger),
            AuthInterceptor(container.AuthService),
        ),
        grpc.MaxRecvMsgSize(4 * 1024 * 1024), // 4MB
        grpc.MaxSendMsgSize(4 * 1024 * 1024), // 4MB
    }
    
    return grpc.NewServer(opts...)
}
```

## Protocol Buffer Best Practices

### Use Proper Field Numbers
```proto
message User {
    string id = 1;      // Never change field numbers
    string name = 2;    // Use sequential numbering
    string email = 3;   // Reserve numbers for future use
    // reserved 4 to 10;
}
```

### Versioning Strategy
```proto
service UserService {
    rpc GetUserV1(GetUserV1Request) returns (GetUserV1Response);
    rpc GetUserV2(GetUserV2Request) returns (GetUserV2Response);
}
```

## Health Checks
Implement gRPC health checking:

```go
import "google.golang.org/grpc/health"
import "google.golang.org/grpc/health/grpc_health_v1"

func registerHealthCheck(server *grpc.Server) {
    healthServer := health.NewServer()
    grpc_health_v1.RegisterHealthServer(server, healthServer)
    
    // Set service status
    healthServer.SetServingStatus("user.UserService", grpc_health_v1.HealthCheckResponse_SERVING)
}
```

## Reflection for Development
Enable gRPC reflection for development:

```go
import "google.golang.org/grpc/reflection"

func enableReflection(server *grpc.Server) {
    reflection.Register(server)
}
```

## Graceful Shutdown
Implement proper shutdown in [cmd/commands/start.go](mdc:cmd/commands/start.go):

```go
func setupGracefulShutdown(server *grpc.Server, logger *log.Logger) {
    sigChan := make(chan os.Signal, 1)
    signal.Notify(sigChan, syscall.SIGINT, syscall.SIGTERM)
    
    go func() {
        <-sigChan
        logger.Println("Shutting down gRPC server...")
        
        // Give requests 30 seconds to finish
        done := make(chan struct{})
        go func() {
            server.GracefulStop()
            close(done)
        }()
        
        select {
        case <-done:
            logger.Println("Server stopped gracefully")
        case <-time.After(30 * time.Second):
            logger.Println("Force stopping server")
            server.Stop()
        }
    }()
}
```

## Testing gRPC Services
Use bufconn for testing without network:

```go
func TestUserService(t *testing.T) {
    buffer := 101024 * 1024
    listener := bufconn.Listen(buffer)
    
    server := grpc.NewServer()
    pb.RegisterUserServiceServer(server, &UserHandler{})
    
    go func() {
        server.Serve(listener)
    }()
    defer server.Stop()
    
    conn, err := grpc.DialContext(ctx, "", grpc.WithContextDialer(func(context.Context, string) (net.Conn, error) {
        return listener.Dial()
    }), grpc.WithInsecure())
    
    client := pb.NewUserServiceClient(conn)
    // Test your service...
}
```
